{"t": 478.08, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 2, "k": 1, "move": "modify_topology", "name": "sshi_fbr_res", "rationale": "The previous SSHI FBR design delivered sufficient power (vavg > 1.8V) but suffered from high output ripple (vpp) and slow settling (dv) on marginal conditions (S2, S4). The ripple is dominated by the high-energy charge bursts transferred from Cp to the storage capacitor C1 during the synchronous flip. Adding a small series resistor (R_smooth) between the rectifier output and the storage capacitor limits these peak currents, reducing vpp without significantly increasing the DC settling time (since R_smooth << RL).", "circuit": {"move": "modify_topology", "name": "sshi_fbr_res", "rationale": "The previous SSHI FBR design delivered sufficient power (vavg > 1.8V) but suffered from high output ripple (vpp) and slow settling (dv) on marginal conditions (S2, S4). The ripple is dominated by the high-energy charge bursts transferred from Cp to the storage capacitor C1 during the synchronous flip. Adding a small series resistor (R_smooth) between the rectifier output and the storage capacitor limits these peak currents, reducing vpp without significantly increasing the DC settling time (since R_smooth << RL).", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "value": 0.002}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "n_rect"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "n_rect"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "R_smooth", "type": "R", "nodes": ["n_rect", "out"], "value": 10.0}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 2.2e-06}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
